#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:51
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "A single claim made once, right after scoping and before the parallel fork. Unlike the per-edit lifecycle in editing-hci-validation, this diagram seeds one bean for the whole DAK and never returns here to log or resolve it, so tracking any one track's own progress is not this lane's concern."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:214
#. Diagram label
msgid "Assemble and validate the DAK"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:215
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Assemble the validated components and run content validation: schemas, cross-component consistency and terminology bindings. The smart-base extractors read the authored artefacts; with SMART_BASE_HOME unset they report skip, never a clean run."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:168
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the component's indicators and its functional and non-functional requirements. These are the DAK's requirements, distinct from skills/requirements/*.json, which are this harness's own conformance obligations. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the indicators-and-requirements inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: each names the persona and process it serves and traces to L1; renderer: prose diff; reviewer: business analyst with the programme manager)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:141
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the DAK's L2 business processes as BPMN 2.0, with Diagram Interchange: a .bpmn with no x/y on its shapes parses and renders blank. Stay at L2 — reviewable by a clinician, not FHIR. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the BPMN inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: bpmn-js import with no warnings, dak-swimlanes.ts, artefact-reachability; renderer: render:bpmn with a visual-diff before/after; reviewer: clinical SME)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:132
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the DAK's personas and the user journeys (scenarios) they appear in, then have them reviewed: calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the personas-and-scenarios inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: dak-swimlanes.ts and traceability to L1 recommendations; renderer: the persona card and a prose diff; reviewer: clinical SME). These are the DAK's own actors, not this harness's scenarios/roles.json — the two vocabularies must not be conflated."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:159
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the data dictionary and core data elements for this component. Stay structured but not FHIR: a data element a clinician can review, from which L3 can later be derived rather than written twice. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the glossary inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: check-web-annexes.ts, on the data dictionary web annex; renderer: the term diff from dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts and each form's chosen wireframe; reviewer: clinical SME, terminologist for codes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:150
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the decision and scheduling logic as DMN tables, within the FEEL subset the interpreter implements (any, literals, comparisons, one-of). Ranges, not() and function calls are refused at load, so write inside the subset. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the DMN inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: load, reachability, test cases; renderer: dmn2html table before/after, each rule beside its L1 citation; reviewer: clinical SME)."
msgstr ""

