#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:195
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clinical validation and assembly start together. Adjudication is QA, not a gate (owner, 2026-10-14: \"once agent produces L2 it can produce L3\"): the DAK is assembled and handed to L3 while the SME reviews it, and a \"changes needed\" sends the work round again, which re-assembles it."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clinical validation runs beside assembly, not before it: it is QA, not a gate (owner, 2026-10-14). A \"no\" here does not return to the specific task that erred but loops back through Gateway_AuthorMerge into the fork itself, so this lane's judgement — not the analyst's — decides whether personas, BPMN, DMN, data dictionary and indicators all get revisited together."
msgstr ""

