#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Enumerate the processes, decisions and data elements the guideline implies; identify the actors."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:201
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Ground truth: does the DAK say what the guideline says? This is the whole-DAK reading, across components: whether the personas, processes, decisions, data elements and indicators tell one consistent story. Each component has already had its own review, forking off inside its track (Process_L2ComponentEditReview, skill l2-component-edit-review), so this step does not repeat those per-component reviews."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a WHO SMART Guidelines L2 Digital Adaptation Kit is authored by a business analyst, a terminologist and a clinical SME under a programme manager. folio-assistant — authoring a WHO SMART Guidelines L2 Digital Adaptation Kit. Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The <bootstrap.processes:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill that implements it; <cat-harness.processes:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared work plan in beans/. Each of the six authoring tracks is a call into l2-component-edit-review.bpmn (Process_L2ComponentEditReview): the agent edits the component, checks, renders and stages it, and hands it on, while a person in the component's reviewing role reviews it alongside, never as a gate. The track's renderer, checker and reviewer are tabled in the skill l2-component-edit-review."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:177
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "ICD-11, SNOMED CT, LOINC bindings — governed separately from the artifacts that cite them. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the terminology inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: bindings resolve and unmappedConcepts is reported; renderer: the term diff on the code columns; reviewer: a terminologist other than the one who bound it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:167
#. Diagram label
msgid "Indicators and requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Ingest the DAK into the library; it is L2, so it gets no L1 graph. Read Component 1 §1.2 for the sources it draws on (extract-dak-l1-references.ts --context-only), then fetch each L1 source on its own — fetch-dspace-item.ts for an IRIS handle, fetch-who-publication.ts for a who.int item page — and ingest it. Record whether each is L1 on its intake (declared > context > inferred; --record-context writes §1.2's context). For each L1 source, run l1-specialise.ts: its publication, sections and elements as specialisations of its library nodes, since the library is upstream of L1. Validate with the smart-base Zod validator. Fidelity — does each citation name the source it resolves to — and a cited edition older than the one fetched are left to a person, never passed automatically."
msgstr ""

