#. Diagram label
msgid "not yours"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:241
#. Diagram label
msgid "Not yours — left alone"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:76
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One parallel branch of the fork, producing bindings the other five tracks cite rather than author themselves, and calling the same edit-and-review subprocess as they do, with a different terminologist as its reviewer. Kept a separate lane rather than folded into the analyst's because governance of a code binding is deliberately independent of the artefact that cites it."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:229
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the bean"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:59
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Opens the parallel fork into six authoring tracks — five landing here, the sixth (terminology) crossing into a separate lane — and re-enters that same fork whenever clinical validation sends work back, so a fix after Gateway_Accurate revisits every track it is entangled with rather than patching only the one SME flagged. Performs the assemble-and-validate in parallel with clinical validation, not after it (owner, 2026-10-14: adjudication is QA, not a gate), and again after any rework. Before any of that, and before the work plan is seeded, builds the DAK's L1 library from what its Component 1 cites, so every track starts with the guidance it operationalises already in the library and in the L1 graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:131
#. Diagram label
msgid "Personas and scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:246
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanClose: end the bean in a state that says why — complete and archive it, scrap it with its reasons and archive it, or record the blocker and hand it back. The one place resolve and archive are drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); placed straight before the end so the engine's resolve sees nothing left but the archive step."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:230
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Process_BeanOpen: check before you create, find out whose the bean is, and claim it — or leave it alone when it is someone else's. The one place a claim is drawn (bean m8gz, owner 2026-10-24); the gateway after this reads which end it reached."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Programme manager / technical officer"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:236
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Reads which end Process_BeanOpen reached. `claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a human holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops here rather than work a bean it does not own (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

